{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class textdocumentanalysis {\n    static int wordsInBraces = 0;\n    static int longestWordLength = 0;\n\n    static int countWords(String s) {\n        s = s.replace(\"_\", \" \");\n        s = s.trim().replaceAll(\"\\\\s+\", \" \");\n        String[] arr = s.split(\" \");\n        return (arr.length == 1 && arr[0].isEmpty()) ? 0 : arr.length;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scan = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = scan.nextInt();\n        scan.nextLine();\n        String line = scan.nextLine();\n        \n        List<Integer> bracketIndices = new ArrayList<>();\n        bracketIndices.add(-1);\n        \n        for (int idx = 0; idx < line.length(); idx++) {\n            char c = line.charAt(idx);\n            if (c == '(' || c == ')') {\n                bracketIndices.add(idx);\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int pairIndex = 1;\n        int wordCount = 0;\n        StringBuilder outsideContent = new StringBuilder();\n        \n        while (pairIndex < bracketIndices.size() - 1) {\n            int openIndex = bracketIndices.get(pairIndex);\n            int closeIndex = bracketIndices.get(pairIndex + 1);\n            \n            String inside = line.substring(openIndex + 1, closeIndex);\n            wordCount += countWords(inside);\n            \n            String before = line.substring(bracketIndices.get(pairIndex - 1) + 1, openIndex);\n            outsideContent.append('_').append(before);\n            \n            pairIndex += 2;\n        }\n        \n        String afterLast = line.substring(bracketIndices.get(bracketIndices.size() - 1) + 1);\n        outsideContent.append('_').append(afterLast);\n        \n        String processed = outsideContent.toString()\n                .replace(\"_\", \" \")\n                .trim()\n                .replaceAll(\"\\\\s+\", \" \");\n        \n        String[] wordList = processed.split(\" \");\n        for (String w : wordList) {\n            if (w.length() > longestWordLength) {\n                longestWordLength = w.length();\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.print(longestWordLength + \" \" + wordCount);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nwordsInBraces = 0\nlongestWordLength = 0\n\ndef countWords(s):\n    s = s.replace(\"_\", \" \")\n    s = s.strip().replace(\"\\\\s+\", \" \")\n    # Python doesn't have direct regex replace like Java, so we use split which handles multiple spaces\n    arr = s.split()\n    return 0 if (len(arr) == 1 and arr[0] == \"\") else len(arr)\n\ndef main():\n    global longestWordLength, wordsInBraces\n    \n    n = int(sys.stdin.readline())\n    line = sys.stdin.readline().rstrip('\\n')\n    \n    bracketIndices = []\n    bracketIndices.append(-1)\n    \n    for idx in range(len(line)):\n        c = line[idx]\n        if c == '(' or c == ')':\n            bracketIndices.append(idx)\n    \n    pairIndex = 1\n    wordCount = 0\n    outsideContent = []\n    \n    while pairIndex < len(bracketIndices) - 1:\n        openIndex = bracketIndices[pairIndex]\n        closeIndex = bracketIndices[pairIndex + 1]\n        \n        inside = line[openIndex + 1:closeIndex]\n        wordCount += countWords(inside)\n        \n        before = line[bracketIndices[pairIndex - 1] + 1:openIndex]\n        outsideContent.append('_')\n        outsideContent.append(before)\n        \n        pairIndex += 2\n    \n    afterLast = line[bracketIndices[-1] + 1:]\n    outsideContent.append('_')\n    outsideContent.append(afterLast)\n    \n    processed = ''.join(outsideContent)\n    processed = processed.replace(\"_\", \" \").strip()\n    # Replace multiple spaces with single space\n    while \"  \" in processed:\n        processed = processed.replace(\"  \", \" \")\n    \n    wordList = processed.split(\" \")\n    for w in wordList:\n        if len(w) > longestWordLength:\n            longestWordLength = len(w)\n    \n    print(str(longestWordLength) + \" \" + str(wordCount))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.128461584215984e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.026322508230805397, -0.0018462770385667682, -0.002809508005157113, -0.3988766074180603, -0.011050572618842125, -0.00016211149340961128, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.847726889536716e-05, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -6.270212179515511e-05, -1.1086402082582936e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.0003367095487192273, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.001531738555058837, -5.364403477869928e-06, -2.4199192921514623e-05, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.556489552167477e-06, -0.002229587407782674, -4.768370445162873e-07, -4.768370